-- title:
--   Nilpotence of Tᵣ-θ(Tᵣ) on the localised cohomology
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal and with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$; let $p$ be a prime with $p\neq 2$ and $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$, i.e. a monoid homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)=\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\,\mathbb Q\simeq_{\mathbb Q}\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\,\mathbb Q$ to $\mathrm{End}_k V$ with $\dim_k V=2$, factoring through a finite level, and assume $\bar\rho$ is absolutely irreducible (its base change to $\overline k$ is irreducible). Let $S$ be a finite set of primes containing $p$, let $N\ge 1$ have all its prime divisors in $S$, let $r$ be a prime with $r\notin S$ and $r\nmid N$, and assume the $\mathbb C$-span of the integral lattice in weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ is everything. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism to $k$ from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the Hecke generators away from $S$, and assume that for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit in $P$ and every $\sigma$ that is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $P$ (that is, $\sigma$ lies in the decomposition group of $P$ and acts on the residue field of $P$ by $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$), one has $\mathrm{charpoly}(\bar\rho(\sigma))=X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Finally assume `BaseOpComm N r S 𝒪`: the operators $\mathrm{baseOp}\,g$ on $H^1(N,\top;\mathcal O)=\mathrm{Hom}(\Gamma_0(N)^{\mathrm{ab}},\mathcal O)$ commute pairwise, $g$ running over the index type `Gen N r S`, each of whose elements carries a prime $\ell$ together with $\ell\nmid N$ and $\ell\notin S$. Write $D$ for the resulting Hecke datum `baseHeckeData`, with free algebra $R=\mathcal O[X_g:g\in\,$`Gen N r S`$]$, with $\tilde\theta\colon R\to k$ the $\mathcal O$-algebra map sending $X_g\mapsto\theta(T_{\ell(g)})$, with `opAlgHom` the $\mathcal O$-algebra map $R\to\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal O}H^1$ sending $X_g\mapsto\mathrm{baseOp}\,g$, and with `toML` the localisation map from $H^1$ to $\mathrm{ML}=$`baseML`, the localisation of $H^1$ at the complement of the prime `mTheta` of $R$. Then there exists $z_0\in R$ with $\tilde\theta(z_0)=\theta(T_r)$ and an $n\in\mathbb N$ such that for every $v\in H^1(N,\top;\mathcal O)$ the image in $\mathrm{ML}$ of $\bigl((\,$`heckeTL N ⊤ 𝒪 r`$-\mathrm{opAlgHom}(z_0))^n\bigr)v$ lies in $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}\cdot\mathrm{ML}$.
--
--   This is the statement that on the localisation of $H^1(\Gamma_0(N),\mathcal O)$ at the maximal ideal cut out by $\theta$ the further Hecke operator $T_r$ acts, modulo $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$ and up to nilpotents, through a polynomial in the retained operators with value $\theta(T_r)=\mathrm{tr}\,\bar\rho(\mathrm{Frob}_r)$; it is the arithmetic input showing that omitting $T_r$ from the generators does not change the localised module. It is used in the identification of the corner submodule of `baseML` at squarefree level.
